# Work out the refund

- The refund covers only the items sent back, not the rest of the order {#returned-items-only}
  e.g. two rain jackets and a trail map ordered, one jacket sent back -> 1990 cents, the price of that one jacket
- Each item is refunded at the price on its order line, times the quantity sent back {#price-times-quantity}
  e.g. two pairs of wool socks at 1200 cents sent back -> 2400 cents before any discount
- A discount on the order lowers the refund by the same percentage {#discount-applied}
  e.g. a 2000-cent water bottle on an order with 10 percent off -> 1800 cents
- A refund is a whole number of cents {#whole-cents}
  e.g. a 1990-cent rain jacket on an order with 15 percent off -> 1692 cents, never a fraction of a cent
- The refund is worked out when the return is submitted and stays with it {#amount-set-at-submission}
  e.g. a return submitted for 1800 cents -> still reads 1800 cents once it has been approved and refunded

